      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Portal events/methods/variable request to this:\n`Event` OnPortalSpawn(Portal, VRCPlayerApi)\n`Get/Set` Position/Rotation/Scale (*Security measure for preventing portals being moved on top (near) a player*)\n`Get/Set` Name (*`Set` static portals only*)\n`Get/Set` World Id (*`Get/Set` static portals only*)\n`Get/Set` Type (p, f, f+, i, i+, default) (*`Set` static portals only*)\n`Get/Set` Region (*`Set` static portals only*)\n`Get/Set` IsUnlocked (*`Set` static portals only*)\n`Get/Set` Instance *Link* (set the same owner & nonce so instances can be *linked*) (*`Set` static portals only*)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-26T02:05:34.546Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Portals can currently be accessed by Udon, and their standard Unity components can be manipulated.\nThis is useful functionality that should be preserved, either directly or via a future API.\nThis means Transforms can be moved, colliders can be switched off, and renderers can be manipulated.\nI've used this ability to:\n- change all properties of transforms in the portal's hierarchy\n- enable and disable gameObjects' active state within the portal's hierarchy\n- get gameObject names in the hierarrchy\n- enable and disable renderer components\n- enable and disable collider components\nUdon does not have access to the destination of portals or any properties of the internal scripts. Any request for that functionality is outside the scope of this request.",
